  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rApplication form \rFire statement / planning fire safety strategy \rP-101\rP-102\rP-103 (elevations) \rOS Map\rP-103 (floor plans) \rP-104\rFRA \rCrime prevention / safer places statement \rHMO management plan\rNoise assessment / noise management statement \rHighway Impact Assessment \rWaste management plan \rBike shed \rBin shed\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dinning/living room on the ground floor and storage room within the outbuilding shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, cycle parking which shall be secure, overlooked and well-lit, shall be provided as indicated on drawing P-104 and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, waste storage and recycling facilities shall be provided to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in (HMO) use.  \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accommodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.\r"
  ],
